[inference]
template_type: KnowAct
contract:
  input:
    trace_dir_n: string
    task: string
    gap_analysis: array
    proposed_diff: array
    proptest_dispatches: array
    evidence_cited: array
    rationale: string
  output:
    summary: string
    files_changed: array
    expected_mutants_killed: array
    expected_bugs_caught: array
    cost_estimate: string
    next_iteration_focus: string
visibility: Public
---
{# Template: harness-optimize/harness-optimize-report.j2 #}
{# Structured report of proposed test changes #}

[inference]
temperature = 0.1
work_effort = "medium"
verbosity = "standard"
max_tokens = 4096
thinking_budget = "standard"

You are a test harness reporter. Compile the proposed test improvements into
a structured report.

## Task

{{ task }}

## Trace Directory (revision N)

{{ trace_dir_n }}

## Gap Analysis

{{ gap_analysis | tojson }}

## Proposed Diff

{{ proposed_diff | tojson }}

## Proptest Dispatches

{{ proptest_dispatches | tojson }}

## Evidence Cited

{{ evidence_cited | tojson }}

## Rationale

{{ rationale }}

## Instructions

Compile the report. For each proposed change:
- Identify which mutants it should kill (from the surviving_mutants list)
- Identify which bugs it should catch (from bug-hunt findings or failures)
- Estimate the CI runtime cost (Pareto: quality vs cost — Meta-Harness paper)
- Suggest what the next iteration should focus on if this diff is accepted

Output a JSON object with:
- `summary`: one-paragraph summary of the proposed improvements
- `files_changed`: array of file paths that will be created or modified
- `expected_mutants_killed`: array of mutant descriptions that the new tests should kill
- `expected_bugs_caught`: array of bug descriptions that the new tests should catch
- `cost_estimate`: approximate CI runtime for the new tests
- `next_iteration_focus`: what to focus on if this diff is accepted and the loop continues